What: read each KMS BGR0 row once into reusable cached row-pair scratch,
convert with libyuv to owned NV12, and copy to independent encoder frames.
Only even unscaled/unpadded BT.601 limited 8-bit V4L2 H.264 consumers may
request it. Visible cursors, mixed negotiation and unsupported cases retain
RGB plus swscale. Remove inherited rotation timing probes and all observers.
Status: experimental ARM optimization; libyuv supplies its NEON dispatch.
Evidence: cec8d8a, 6b81298, e1180ed; /tmp/h700-sun/convert.md (2026-10-22).
The row-pair-test.cpp compares exact pixels to whole-frame libyuv, padding,
unaligned source and invalid geometry. libyuv differs slightly from swscale.
Removal: equivalent upstream conversion, accepted hardware conversion, or
unsafe colour/lifetime evidence. See services/sunshine/README.md.

